    "risk_level": "Low to Medium",
    "energy_cost": "Medium",
    "time_sustainability": "Medium to Long"
  },
  "state_invariants": [
    "Chest-to-chest or chest-to-side connection maintained with opponent's torso, creating constant pressure through the sternum and shoulder girdle while eliminating space between bodies",
    "Opponent's guard is fully passed with hips cleared past opponent's knee line, ensuring no leg entanglement or opportunity for guard recovery exists",
    "Top player is positioned perpendicularly or at a slight angle (45-90 degrees) to opponent's longitudinal axis, with weight distributed across opponent's chest and diaphragm area",
    "Head control established either directly through crossface pressure driving opponent's face away, or indirectly through shoulder pressure and arm positioning that restricts head movement"
  ],
  "prerequisites": [
    "Successful guard pass with hips fully cleared past opponent's legs",
    "Control of opponent's upper body through crossface, underhook, or head position",
    "Prevention of guard recovery with proper hip positioning and base",
    "Stability in base with knees and hips positioned to distribute weight effectively"
  ],
  "key_principles": [
    "Distribute weight strategically across opponent's chest and hips using shoulder pressure, chest weight, and hip positioning to maximize control while maintaining mobility",
    "Eliminate space between bodies through constant pressure and connection, preventing opponent from creating frames or inserting defensive structures",
    "Control opponent's head and far-side arm using crossface, underhook, or gift wrap positions to limit their mobility and escape options",
    "Maintain low center of gravity with hips close to the mat and weight settled into opponent rather than posted high on hands",
    "Use shoulder pressure to restrict breathing and movement by driving shoulder into opponent's jaw or neck area",
    "Create and maintain multiple points of control simultaneously, never relying on single control points that can be easily defeated",
    "Apply constant pressure while remaining mobile and ready to transition between side control variations or advance to dominant positions"
  ],
